  "title": "Provider-neutral tracker seam and the GitHub adapter",
  "summary": "Adds a provider-neutral `Tracker` seam to the osf crate: a trait with read/write/capability operations, a ready rule that decides which read item may be dispatched, a finishing sequence that checks capabilities before writing state and recap, and an in-memory test double. The first adapter, `GitHubTracker`, implements the seam over GitHub Issues and Projects v2 by shelling out to `gh` — one process per request, with pure argv/payload builders and pure response parsers, plus a real runner that drains pipes on threads and enforces a 60-second timeout.",
